{"name":"Folk Guitar","hex":"#7a634f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"folk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A people; a tribe or nation; the inhabitants of a region, especially the native inhabitants.","People, persons."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to the inhabitants of a land, their culture, tradition, or history.","Of or pertaining to common people as opposed to ruling classes or elites."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/folk"},{"term":"guitar","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A stringed musical instrument, of European origin, usually with a fretted fingerboard and six strings, played with the fingers or a plectrum (guitar pick).","Any type of musical instrument of the lute family, characterized by a flat back, along with a neck whose upper surface is in the same plane as the soundboard, with strings along the neck and parallel to the soundboard."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To play the guitar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guitar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Steel-string acoustic guitar","blocks":[{"text":"The steel-string acoustic guitar is one of the most common forms of modern guitars, descending from the original gut-strung Romantic guitar. Unlike classical Spanish guitars, which typically have nylon strings, modern acoustic guitars are strung with steel strings for a brighter, louder sound. The steel-string is often referred simply as an acoustic guitar or a folk guitar."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Gibson_SJ200.jpg/330px-Gibson_SJ200.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steel-string_acoustic_guitar"},{"title":"Guitar","blocks":[{"text":"The guitar is a stringed musical instrument that is usually fretted and typically has six or twelve strings, though guitars with seven, eight and nine strings also exist. It is usually held flat against the player's body and played by strumming or plucking the strings with the dominant hand, while simultaneously pressing selected strings against frets with the fingers of the opposite hand. A guitar pick may also be used to strike the strings. The sound of the guitar is projected either acoustically, by means of a resonant hollow chamber on the guitar, or amplified by an electronic pickup and an amplifier."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/GuitareClassique5.png/330px-GuitareClassique5.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guitar"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Playing_acoustic_guitar.jpg/500px-Playing_acoustic_guitar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Playing_acoustic_guitar.jpg/500px-Playing_acoustic_guitar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fingerpicking a steel-string guitar","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlaying_acoustic_guitar.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/C.F._Martin_000-28EC_Eric_Clapton_model_Acoustic_Guitar.jpg/500px-C.F._Martin_000-28EC_Eric_Clapton_model_Acoustic_Guitar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/C.F._Martin_000-28EC_Eric_Clapton_model_Acoustic_Guitar.jpg/1280px-C.F._Martin_000-28EC_Eric_Clapton_model_Acoustic_Guitar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/C.F._Martin_000-28EC_Eric_Clapton_model_Acoustic_Guitar.jpg/500px-C.F._Martin_000-28EC_Eric_Clapton_model_Acoustic_Guitar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A C.F. Martin Eric Clapton